Package: gemcox
Title: Gaussian Mixture of Cox Models for Mechanism Subgroups
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Ziwei", "Zhao", email = "zhaoziwe@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits a Gaussian mixture of Cox proportional hazards models
    ('GeM-Cox') to find latent subgroups whose survival mechanisms differ.
    Clustering features follow a Gaussian mixture with diagonal covariance;
    each subgroup has its own Cox coefficient vector over a shared Breslow
    baseline hazard. Estimation is by an EM algorithm whose E-step weights
    the survival likelihood by a fixed exponent gamma. Membership weights for
    new subjects are computed from the clustering features only. Two
    subgroups are tested against one by an in-sample likelihood ratio
    calibrated by a parametric bootstrap; a cross-validated partial
    likelihood statistic (Verweij and van Houwelingen, 1993,
    <doi:10.1002/sim.4780122407>) is also available. A step-by-step workflow
    (read_data(), fit_model(), runCV(), finalModel(), plot_beta_heatmap())
    follows the GeMLR package.
